# Dynamic element conversion before a write

Verifies converting a dynamically indexed element to another unit works without
any prior write: the stored `2cm` converts to the requested millimeters through
the same rule a standalone centimeter value would use, yielding `20mm`.

>>> source
let sizes: int[] = [10mm, 2cm]
let index = 1
print(sizes[index]->to(mm))

<<< stdout
20mm

<<< stderr
